# 56. DESIGN PRINCIPLES

Follow these principles:

1. Simple before clever.
2. Information hierarchy before decoration.
3. Reusable components before one-off components.
4. Clear actions before visual novelty.
5. Student-first learning experience.
6. Teacher-first content creation.
7. Administrator-first visibility and control.
8. Network features should feel trustworthy.
9. Privacy must be obvious.
10. Mobile learning must be excellent.
11. Accessibility is not optional.
12. Every page must have a clear purpose.
13. Every action must have clear feedback.
14. Avoid dashboard overload.
15. Avoid unnecessary modal usage.
16. Avoid excessive card layouts.
17. Make data dense interfaces readable.
18. Make learning interfaces distraction-free.

