# 61. FINAL COMMAND

After inspecting the repository:

1. Build the complete information architecture.
2. Build the design system.
3. Build the complete screen inventory.
4. Create detailed wireframes for every screen.
5. Create role-specific navigation.
6. Create all major user flows.
7. Create responsive versions.
8. Create all important states.
9. Create the route architecture.
10. Map screens to components.
11. Map components to data/domain entities.
12. Separate MVP from post-MVP.
13. Identify inconsistencies or gaps.
14. Recommend improvements before implementation.

Do NOT start coding immediately.

First produce the **complete UX/wireframe specification**.

Then, after the specification is reviewed, implementation can proceed screen-by-screen in vertical slices.

The ultimate objective is not merely to add pages.

The objective is to make **Decimal Tuition feel like a complete, coherent education product that can eventually operate as a standalone product while remaining deeply integrated with Decimal School Management.**
